{"answer": "{
  "summary": "Draft behavioral regression tests for the dma_observer research ARM pulse, extending tests/dma_p4m_observer_test.cpp. The tests sample research_arm_o while cfg_valid_i/cfg_write_i are high, before the command clock edge, and assert: exact accepted P4M ARM pulse when ResearchEnable=1, no pulse when ResearchEnable=0, no pulse on poll/read events, repeated ARM while armed, legacy/non-P4M ARM, partial-strobe ARM, zero-target ARM, and ARM while busy. No production RTL edit is included here; the tests assume Codex's intended dma_observer.sv change is applied.",
  "assumptions": [
    "Production fix is applied in cva6/corev_apu/fpga/src/dma_observer.sv: research_arm_o is initialized to 0 in the main always_comb and set to ResearchEnable && cfg_wdata_i[30] exclusively in the accepted ARM command branch.",
    "tests/test_dma_p4m_observer.py already builds the research variant with -GResearchEnable=1 -GE3Enable=0 -GControlledEnable=0 and runs Vdma_observer with argv 'research'.",
    "The existing non-research P4M variant remains built with ResearchEnable=0; the new accepted-pulse assertion expects research_arm_o==0 there.",
    "The new tests are behavioral event-cycle checks, not timing/path checks. They validate the intended functional contract and must not be replaced by source-string checks."
  ],
  "edits": [
    {
      "path": "tests/dma_p4m_observer_test.cpp",
      "old": "    void write(unsigned addr,uint64_t v){d.cfg_valid_i=d.cfg_write_i=1;d.cfg_addr_i=addr;d.cfg_wdata_i=v;tick();d.cfg_valid_i=d.cfg_write_i=0;d.eval();}\n    uint64_t read(unsigned addr){d.cfg_addr_i=addr;d.eval();return d.cfg_rdata_o;}",
      "new": "    void write(unsigned addr,uint64_t v){d.cfg_valid_i=d.cfg_write_i=1;d.cfg_addr_i=addr;d.cfg_wdata_i=v;tick();d.cfg_valid_i=d.cfg_write_i=0;d.eval();}\n    bool write_pulse(unsigned addr,uint64_t v,unsigned strb=255){\n        d.cfg_valid_i=d.cfg_write_i=1;d.cfg_addr_i=addr;d.cfg_wdata_i=v;d.cfg_wstrb_i=strb;d.eval();\n        bool pulse=d.research_arm_o!=0;\n        tick();\n        d.cfg_valid_i=d.cfg_write_i=0;d.eval();\n        return pulse;\n    }\n    uint64_t read(unsigned addr){d.cfg_addr_i=addr;d.eval();return d.cfg_rdata_o;}"
    },
    {
      "path": "tests/dma_p4m_observer_test.cpp",
      "old": "        b.arm_p4m(0,1,1);\n        b.tick(2);\n        check(((b.status()>>40)&1)!=0&&(b.bank(12)&2)!=0,\"new arm preserves sticky lane error evidence\");\n        cases++;\n    }",
      "new": "        b.arm_p4m(0,1,1);\n        b.tick(2);\n        check(((b.status()>>40)&1)!=0&&(b.bank(12)&2)!=0,\"new arm preserves sticky lane error evidence\");\n        cases++;\n\n        // Research arm output contract: pulse exactly on an accepted P4M ARM command cycle,\n        // never on polls, readback, rejected arms or legacy arms. The accepted-cycle pulse is\n        // sampled while cfg_valid_i is high, before the command's clock edge.\n        b.reset();\n        b.d.batch_active_i=3;\n        b.write(0x68,1);\n        {\n            uint64_t w=1ULL|(1ULL<<30)|(1ULL<<25);\n            bool pulse=b.write_pulse(0x60,w);\n            check(pulse==research,\"research arm pulse follows ResearchEnable on accepted P4M ARM\");\n            check(b.status()==1,\"research P4M ARM accepted\");\n        }\n        check(b.d.research_arm_o==0,\"research arm is low after the accepted command cycle\");\n        b.poll(0,0x77);\n        check(b.d.research_arm_o==0,\"poll does not false-arm research\");\n        b.d.ar_valid_i=b.d.ar_ready_i=1; b.d.rlast_fire_i=1; b.tick();\n        b.d.ar_valid_i=b.d.ar_ready_i=b.d.rlast_fire_i=0;\n        check(b.d.research_arm_o==0,\"read event does not false-arm research\");\n        {\n            uint64_t w=1ULL|(1ULL<<30)|(1ULL<<25);\n            bool pulse=b.write_pulse(0x60,w);\n            check(!pulse,\"repeated ARM while armed does not pulse\");\n            check(((b.status()>>32)&1)!=0,\"repeated ARM while armed is rejected\");\n        }\n\n        b.reset();\n        b.d.batch_active_i=3;\n        b.write(0x68,1);\n        {\n            uint64_t w=1ULL|(1ULL<<25);\n            bool pulse=b.write_pulse(0x60,w);\n            check(!pulse,\"legacy ARM does not pulse research\");\n            check(b.status()==1,\"legacy ARM accepted\");\n        }\n\n        b.reset();\n        b.d.batch_active_i=3;\n        b.write(0x68,1);\n        {\n            uint64_t w=1ULL|(1ULL<<30)|(1ULL<<25);\n            bool pulse=b.write_pulse(0x60,w,1);\n            check(!pulse,\"partial-strobe ARM does not pulse research\");\n            check(((b.status()>>32)&1)!=0,\"partial-strobe ARM rejected\");\n        }\n\n        b.reset();\n        b.d.batch_active_i=3;\n        b.write(0x68,0);\n        {\n            uint64_t w=1ULL|(1ULL<<30)|(1ULL<<25);\n            bool pulse=b.write_pulse(0x60,w);\n            check(!pulse,\"zero-target ARM does not pulse research\");\n            check(((b.status()>>32)&1)!=0,\"zero-target ARM rejected\");\n        }\n\n        b.reset();\n        b.arm_p4m(0,-1,1);\n        b.issue(0,1);\n        {\n            uint64_t w=1ULL|(1ULL<<30)|(1ULL<<25);\n            bool pulse=b.write_pulse(0x60,w);\n            check(!pulse,\"ARM while busy does not pulse research\");\n            check(((b.status()>>32)&1)!=0,\"ARM while busy is rejected\");\n        }\n        cases+=6;\n    }"
    }
  ],
  "commands": [
    "python3 tests/test_dma_p4m_observer.py",
    "python3 tests/test_dma_observer.py"
  ]
